WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.393
It only looks smaller.

2
00:00:01.553 --> 00:00:03.875
Nothing shrinks when it walks away from you.

3
00:00:04.035 --> 00:00:07.750
It only looks smaller, and a drawing shows what things look like.

4
00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:11.440
The same lamp post can be tall, then half as tall, then a thumbnail.

5
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.440
One vanishing point.

6
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.919
Draw a street going away and the two edges of the road head for the same spot.

7
00:00:18.079 --> 00:00:21.283
So do the tops of the houses and the line of lamp posts.

8
00:00:21.443 --> 00:00:27.481
That spot sits on the horizon, level with your own eyes, and it is called the vanishing point.

9
00:00:28.181 --> 00:00:29.527
Guide lines first.

10
00:00:29.687 --> 00:00:30.709
Start light.

11
00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:34.538
Thin, pale lines find where things go, and you can still move them.

12
00:00:34.698 --> 00:00:37.995
Compare sizes by holding your pencil out at arm's length.

13
00:00:38.155 --> 00:00:39.688
The darks go in last.

14
00:00:40.388 --> 00:00:41.456
Near and far.

15
00:00:41.616 --> 00:00:46.538
Near things are bigger, lower down the page, full of detail and drawn darkest.

16
00:00:46.698 --> 00:00:49.949
Far things are smaller, higher up, pale and plain.

17
00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:52.478
Use all four and your picture has depth.
